{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/edgedepthfirstsearchevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/EdgeSearchEvents.swift#L37","fileName":"EdgeSearchEvents.swift"},"symbolKind":"enum","title":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent","externalID":"s:9Traversal25EdgeDepthFirstSearchEventO"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A vertex is discovered, then its out-edges are reported, then it is finished. An edge to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"undiscovered vertex is a tree edge, and the search continues from that vertex before the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge. An edge to a vertex discovered but not yet finished is a back edge; a self-loop is one.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An edge to a finished vertex is a forward edge when that vertex was discovered later than the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex being explored, and a cross edge otherwise.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a directed graph every out-edge of an explored vertex is reported. In an undirected graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each edge is reported once, from the end that reaches it first: the tree edge is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported again from the vertex it discovered, but a parallel edge to the parent is a back edge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a self-loop is one back edge. Without pruning or a depth limit an undirected search has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only tree and back edges; an edge to a finished vertex whose edges were not explored is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forward or cross edge."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/SQ","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/SH","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/backEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/crossEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/discover(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/finish(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/forwardEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/treeEdge(_:)"],"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What an edge depth-first search reports, in order: the events of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"type":"text","text":", with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each edge given by its position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", so parallel edges are told apart."}],"references":{"doc://Traversal/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://Traversal/documentation/Traversal":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal","type":"topic","title":"Traversal","abstract":[],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/traversal","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traversal/s9EscapableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/s9EscapableP","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://Traversal/documentation/Traversal/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent/discover(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/traversal\/edgedepthfirstsearchevent\/discover(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/discover(_:)","kind":"symbol","title":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent.discover(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","te